<header class="sg-head"><p class="featured-region">Dance · date unknown · Oceania</p><h1 class="sg-title">Taba Naba</h1><p class="sg-kid" data-say>A children's song from the Torres Strait Islands, sung sitting down, with hand movements that act out a trip to the reef.</p></header>
<dl class="sg-facts"><div><dt>Words</dt><dd>traditional</dd></div><div><dt>Music</dt><dd>traditional</dd></div><div><dt>Culture</dt><dd>Torres Strait Islanders</dd></div><div><dt>Language</dt><dd>Meriam Mir</dd></div><div><dt>Place</dt><dd>Torres Strait Islands, Australia</dd></div><div><dt>Date</dt><dd>traditional; date not known</dd></div><div><dt>Type</dt><dd>Dance</dd></div><div><dt>The words</dt><dd>Public domain (traditional Torres Strait Islander song; authors not known)</dd></div></dl>
<div class="sg-body">
<section class="sg-sec" id="story"><h2>The story</h2><p>&quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taba-naba">Taba Naba</a>&quot; is a traditional children's song of the Torres Strait Islands, just north of the Australian mainland, sung in Meriam Mir, a language of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torres-strait-islanders">Torres Strait Islanders</a>. It is usually accompanied by a &quot;sit-down dance&quot;, in which the dancers stay seated and perform traditional movements that match the words.</p><p>The song reached a wide audience when the children's band The Wiggles performed it with the Australian pop singer Christine Anu, a native of the eastern Torres Strait, on their album It's a Wiggly Wiggly World (2000); in the video Anu performed the sit-down dance. It was later featured in two of the band's television series, Lights, Camera, Action, Wiggles! and Ready, Steady, Wiggle!, and in Wiggle Town and Duets, with Anu returning. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> the singer Xuxa recorded it for her album Xuxa Só Para Baixinhos 4.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="meaning"><h2>What it says</h2><p>An invitation to go out to the reef: the singers call one another to get into the dinghy when the morning tide is low and row out to the reef's edge. The seated dancers act out the words with their arms and hands. The mood is cheerful and lively.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="words"><h2>The words</h2><p class="sg-nowords sg-nowords-g" data-say>The words of this song are in the public domain, but no free, reliable edition has been found yet to import them from, and the Institute never types a song&#8217;s words from memory: Genius shows them below, under its own licence.</p><div class="sg-genius"><div class="sg-genius-btns"><button type="button" class="sg-genius-btn" data-genius="10578862" data-what="Lyrics">Show the lyrics from Genius</button></div><div class="sg-genius-frames"></div><p class="sg-genius-note">Genius shows the lyrics in its own frame, under its own licence: nothing loads from Genius until you press a button. <a href="https://genius.com/The-wiggles-taba-naba-lyrics" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The song on Genius</a>.</p></div></section>
</div>
<section class="sg-sec" id="listen"><h2>Listen</h2><div class="sg-video" data-yt="58Xn9bTIxGI" data-title="Taba Naba: Christine Anu with The Wiggles, with the sit-down dance"><button type="button" class="sg-play"><span class="sg-play-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="sg-play-t">Play the performance</span><span class="sg-play-n">Christine Anu with The Wiggles, with the sit-down dance</span></button></div><p class="sg-video-cr">On YouTube, from the channel The Wiggles. Pressing play loads YouTube&#8217;s player. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=58Xn9bTIxGI" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch on YouTube<span aria-hidden="true"> &#8599;</span></a></p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">It's a Wiggly Wiggly World (The Wiggles, with Christine Anu)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2000</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recorded, with a video of the sit-down dance</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Xuxa Só Para Baixinhos 4 (Xuxa)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recorded on an album</span></li></ul></section>
